Reason:
The `admin.addCluster(clusterName, false);` statement attempts to add the cluster without ensuring that it is fully initialized. This can lead to a situation where subsequent calls to `getInstancesInCluster(clusterName)` fail because the cluster is not ready, resulting in the AMS stopping unexpectedly after a rolling upgrade.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
boolean success = false;
for (int i = 0; i < tries && !success; i++) {
    List<String> nodes = admin.getInstancesInCluster(clusterName);
}
```
Reason:
The addition of a retry mechanism with a loop that attempts to retrieve the instances in the cluster allows the system to wait until the Helix cluster is fully set up before proceeding. This prevents failures when trying to add instances to an uninitialized cluster, thereby ensuring proper functionality after a rolling upgrade.

